    "caveats": [
      "PM2.5 in Delhi comes from many sources (traffic, industry, dust, local burning, weather). Stubble smoke is one of them.",
      "The index models smoke from the replayed districts only, not all of Punjab and Haryana.",
      "Both series depend on the mixing height: a shallow layer raises the index by construction and also traps PM2.5 from every source, so part of the agreement is shared weather.",
      "The index is relative and has no units; a correlation says how the two move together, not how much PM2.5 the smoke adds."
